:" Positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< P_s"},{"type":"text","text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order and within one in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P_s + q"},{"type":"text","text":" is target incidence "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":", in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order. A per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LabeledGraph law."}]},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedges: ","type":"text"},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"predecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"inHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So graph algorithms run on the view without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hashing a vertex. The view does not offer ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose contract needs edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions in row order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Costs.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", and a vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/directedincidencegraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView\/OutEdges"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","